{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"effect size effect size","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md","fileName":"Effect Size.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Effect Size","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Statistical Power and Effect Size]] · [[Statistical Inference and Resampling]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Statistical Power and Effect Size","Statistical Inference and Resampling","Confidence Interval","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"effect size effect size","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md","fileName":"Effect Size.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Effect Size","heading":"Effect Size","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An effect size quantifies the magnitude of a difference or relationship independently of the sample's p-value. It may be expressed as a standardized mean difference, a raw mean difference, a difference in proportions, a correlation, or a model-specific measure.\n\nPower calculations require an assumed effect size because a study cannot be sized for significance in the abstract. Plausible values should come from scientific relevance, prior evidence, or a transparent sensitivity range rather than from the observed study result alone.\n\nIn the source's two-group examples, the raw difference in sample means is the observed effect. Reporting it with a [[Confidence Interval]] prevents a small p-value from being mistaken for a scientifically important result when a large sample detects a negligible difference.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Statistical Power and Effect Size","Statistical Inference and Resampling","Confidence Interval","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"effect size effect size","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Effect Size.md","fileName":"Effect Size.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Effect Size","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Statistical Power and Effect Size","Statistical Inference and Resampling","Confidence Interval","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}